{"reference":"Isaiah 16","book":"Isaiah","chapter":16,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Within Isaiah","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Isaiah 16 belongs to a wider sequence that addresses foreign nations alongside Judah and Israel. Across Isaiah, nations are judged and held accountable, yet the book also envisions nations learning, worshiping, and sharing in restoration. That wider pattern frames this oracle concerning Moab: its severe portrayal of loss and humiliation is part of a larger book that does not treat the fate of nations in only one way.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_016_7869619b2767e8dde8a20c98"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}